          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP767 - Irma Campground

&lt;strong&gt;Posted:&lt;/strong&gt; N 52° 55.124 W 111° 13.946

&lt;strong&gt;MyGPSr:&lt;/strong&gt; N 52° 55.123 W 111° 13.946&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I decided to take a Sunday drive east to see if I couldn't find this as yet unfound cap. It was rainy off and on during the drive and the sky looked particularly dark over my destination. But as luck would have it when I arrived in Irma there was no rain. Bonus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The campgrounds themselves were deserted with only a dozen people doing some outfield practice at the nearby ball diamond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the quiet gz, the cap was found very quickly and only needed a little dirt trimming and a wipe down to get ready for the photo session. It turned out to be a nice, easy find.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When I was done at the cap,  to make the drive really worth it, with relentless focus, and dogged determination I then found all the caches in the entire town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There was only the one.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_tongue.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap and the excuse for a Sunday drive OFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
